From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:27:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: install SCS and MSCS through NL80211_CMD_SET_SCS/SET_MSCS

The kernel (mac80211 subsys patches 431 to 450) classifies the streams
that a peer requested with SCS and MSCS. It takes the descriptors of an
SCS Request and the MSCS Descriptor element with the classifier elements
as received, and answers each with a status code.

Copy the commands, the attributes and the nested descriptor enums into
nl80211_copy.h, map NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_SCS and _MSCS to
WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_SCS and _MSCS, and add the driver operations set_scs()
and set_mscs(), which install, change or remove one SCS descriptor or the
MSCS of a peer and return the status code of the kernel's reply.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
+++ b/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
@@ -1190,6 +1190,26 @@ int hostapd_drv_set_qos_map(struct hosta
 }
 
 
+int hostapd_drv_set_scs(struct hostapd_data *hapd, const u8 *addr,
+			const struct hostapd_scs_desc *desc, u16 *status)
+{
+	if (!hapd->driver || !hapd->driver->set_scs || !hapd->drv_priv ||
+	    !(hapd->iface->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_SCS))
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	return hapd->driver->set_scs(hapd->drv_priv, addr, desc, status);
+}
+
+
+int hostapd_drv_set_mscs(struct hostapd_data *hapd, const u8 *addr,
+			 const struct hostapd_mscs_desc *desc, u16 *status)
+{
+	if (!hapd->driver || !hapd->driver->set_mscs || !hapd->drv_priv ||
+	    !(hapd->iface->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_MSCS))
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	return hapd->driver->set_mscs(hapd->drv_priv, addr, desc, status);
+}
+
